{{also|Cognac}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fr|cognac}}, from {{m|en|Cognac}}, a city in France, from {{der|en|ML.|Comniacum}}, from the name {{m|la|Cominius}} + Gallo-Roman suffix {{m|la|-acum}}, from {{der|en|cel-pro|*-ākos|*-ākom}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒn.jæk/|/ˈkoʊn.jæk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cognac.wav|Audio (RP)}}
* {{homophones|en|konjac}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Cognac (drink)}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[brandy]] [[distilled]] from [[white wine]] in the [[region]] around [[Cognac]] in [[France]].
#: {{ux|en|Major manufacturers add a small proportion of caramel to color their '''cognacs'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Pete Townshend|authorlink=Pete Townshend|title={{w|Who I Am (book)|Who I Am}}|year=2012|publisher=HarperCollins|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/petetownshendwho0000town/page/265/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-00-746603-0|page=265|passage=We’d have a script meeting for the next day’s shooting that lasted until two in the morning, and he’d be up again at six for a breakfast meeting. I survived on '''cognac'''. I have no idea how he did it.}}

